@dir include/micro-os-plus/micro-test-plus
@brief Folder with C++ header files for the µTest++ Testing Framework.

@details
This folder holds the headers included by the primary public header,
`micro-os-plus/micro-test-plus.h`, which is the only one that the
applications include.

Most of the headers declare what the applications use: the runner
(`runner.h`) and its options (`runner-options.h`), the test suites and
test cases (`test.h`), the counters (`counters.h`), the function
comparators (`function-comparators.h`), the exception checks
(`exceptions.h`), the string utilities (`utility.h`), the concepts and
templates for the application extensions (`extension.h`), the formatter
of the operand values (`expression-formatter.h`), and the deprecated
definitions (`deprecated.h`).

The other headers belong to the implementation, in the `detail`
namespace and the like, and the applications do not need to name their
contents: the check results (`check-result.h`), the reporters
(`reporter.h`, `reporter-human.h`, and `reporter-tap.h`), the shared
templates (`detail.h`), the source location (`reflection.h`), the
mathematical helpers (`math.h`), and the stopwatch (`stopwatch.h`).

The definitions of the inline functions and of the templates are in the
`inlines` subfolder, and the non-inline definitions in the `src` folder.
